=== meta ===
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: `self.assertTrue(True)` in a handler of a test class that is no `unittest.TestCase` raises AttributeError, so the handler does not swallow
origin: #496, a negative for R49's second condition: the class's same-file base chain must reach a base whose name ends in `TestCase`
note: pytest collects `TestValue` without a TestCase base, and there `self` has no `assertTrue`; app.py is unchanged and outside the diff
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


class TestValue:
    def test_value(self):
        assert value() == 1
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


class TestValue:
    def test_value(self):
        try:
            assert value() == 1
        except Exception:
            self.assertTrue(True)
